{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Remediation of the change 2347 blocking `api-compat` finding (patchset 4 = a410fff2698e).\n\nThe finding was REAL, not a false positive. Sweep found TWO affected in-repo consumers, both the same shape (parse `rebar show --output json`, then `isinstance(ts, (int, float))` on the comment `timestamp`), and both FAIL-SOFT — so the break is silent, not loud:\n\n1. `rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.conflict_bug_filing._recent_marker_comment` (the reviewer's finding).\n2. `scripts/alert_dedup.recent_marker_comment` — NOT in the review finding. This is the SHARED dedup primitive behind both scheduled alert lanes (`canary_bridge` x2 call sites, `dependency_audit`), so it is the wider blast radius of the two.\n\nBoth now coerce `int(ts)` when the value is a `str`, which accepts the integer and the decimal-string form alike.\n\nSweep basis (grep for the field names as STRINGS, not only semantic search): every `json.loads` of rebar CLI stdout, plus every `isinstance`/comparison/arithmetic use of `timestamp`/`created_at`/`updated_at`/`signed_at`/`closed_at`. Everything else is unaffected for a STRUCTURAL reason, not by luck — none crosses a CLI JSON boundary:\n- `metrics/bug_trends.py` — in-process `rebar.reduce_ticket()`; library returns arbitrary-precision Python ints.\n- `_commands/compact_plan.py`, `scripts/rebar_duration_probe*.py` — read event/sidecar files straight off disk; `signing.py`'s change touched only the stdout emitters, never the persisted record.\n- `rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py` — uses the timestamp only as an opaque identity key; no typecheck, no arithmetic.\n\nRegression coverage + mutation check: 4 tests in `tests/unit/test_conflict_bug_filing_js_safe_timestamps.py`, 3 in `tests/scripts/test_alert_dedup.py`. Anti-vacuity is asserted in-test (each fixture asserts its instant exceeds 2**53-1 AND that it genuinely serializes as a JSON string), plus a liveness test (a STALE string timestamp must still return False, so a coercion that degenerated to unconditional True would be caught) and a fail-soft test (junk string must not raise). Mutation-checked by reverting each coercion independently and asserting on the RETURN CODE: both mutants KILLED, each by its own consumer's test (1 failed / 16 passed in each case), and the mutation was verified to have actually applied before running.\n\nGates: `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; 30/30 on the affected suites; 3752 passed on the reconciler/conflict unit selection.\n\nAC#3 (drift protection) deliberately left UNTICKED and delegated to `spherelike-oily-honeyeater` (83eb-c3e1-3dfd-472f); no structural guard added here, and `file_impact` deliberately NOT widened, so the certified plan-review attestation stays valid. Description untouched for the same reason.\n\nNote: patchset 4 was pushed by a concurrent session working the same worktree; it carries exactly this remediation with the Change-Id preserved. The prior -1 was cleared and a fresh review/CI is pending (no vote copy — this is a code change, not `changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE`)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787961078007185994,"uuid":"b74b8eb9-ebc9-46d1-8d4e-90a583f72e8f"}